{arial}Station Timbuk 2
Operator: Sergeant Barkod

from: {arialbld}Alex Kolman{arial}
Headquarters of Kapharna 







The largest offensive ever in desert warfare will take place tomorrow. Magnus Von Tekton has ordered total commitment. The Psychos will throw at us everything they have, by land, sea, and air.

Three armies are primed to engage in action. 

From {arialbld}Cairo{arial}, Kurt Rorscham will be assigned the vital mission of containing Tankred's fleet based at {arialbld}Bir-El-Guedima{arial}. 

On your flank at {arialbld}El Alamein{arial}, Bob Renard will charge towards the east on {arialbld}Aswad{arial} so as to overpower Karlo's tarmacs. 

As for you, {rank} {name}, you have the privilege of marching on the capital {arialbld}Jaffa{arial} in the south, currently held by Otton's heavy combat units.

Between {arialbld}Kharthoum{arial} your HQ and Jaffa you might find your best ally: the natural barrier of the Azul mountains, a labyrinth of narrow passes preventing any frontal deployment of Tekton armours.

On such a terrain artillery will be of prime importance.
This reminds me of the report you wrote two months ago, and I quote: "...all our artillery can do against these heavy tanks is remove their dust ...".

It seems like your corrosive words burned our Engineers' egos right where it hurts, as they have been working day and night to conceive a new artillery model with longer range and "a strong dusting effect".












{center}{device7}















Just in time for your birthday, six premier prototypes have arrived at Khartoum.

Good luck {rank}.



{offset150}{arialbld}Alex Kolman{arial}

Glorious Commander of the Normo Cohorts



